# Captures are evidence: their bytes are what a digest is recomputed over. Git's CRLF
# conversion on checkout would change those bytes on another machine and the gate would
# report a digest mismatch on a capture nobody touched. Pinned to LF.
#
# The gate also normalises CRLF before hashing, so this is belt and braces - deliberately,
# because the two failures look identical from the outside (a mismatch) and only one of
# them means what the message says.
*.txt -text eol=lf
